⭐ 6. OAuth Setup Requirements

To use OAuth (Google example), you must:

✔ 1. Go to Google Cloud Console

Create a project

Enable “Google OAuth API”

Create OAuth credentials

Add Redirect URI (e.g., http://localhost:5000/auth/google/callback)

Copy
→ Client ID
→ Client Secret

✔ 2. Install passport or googleapis package
✔ 3. Create routes for login and callback
✔ 4. Validate user and store in DB
✔ 5. Generate your own session/JWT


Configure Passport Strategy
import passport from "passport";
import GoogleStrategy from "passport-google-oauth20";
import User from "./models/User.js"; 

passport.use(
  new GoogleStrategy(
    {
      clientID: process.env.GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID,
      clientSecret: process.env.GOOGLE_SECRET,
      callbackURL: "/auth/google/callback",
    },
    async (accessToken, refreshToken, profile, done) => {
      // find or create user
      let user = await User.findOne({ googleId: profile.id });

      if (!user) {
        user = await User.create({
          googleId: profile.id,
          name: profile.displayName,
          email: profile.emails[0].value,
        });
      }

      return done(null, user);
    }
  )
);

passport.serializeUser((user, done) => {
  done(null, user.id);
});

passport.deserializeUser(async (id, done) => {
  const user = await User.findById(id);
  done(null, user);
});


. OAuth Example Answer
“OAuth is used for secure third-party login like Google or GitHub.
It allows users to log in without sharing passwords.

I implemented Google OAuth using PassportJS in Node.js. 
I configured a Google OAuth strategy with Client ID and Secret.

When a user clicks login, they are redirected to Google’s consent page.
Google returns an authorization code, which my backend exchanges for an access token. 
I use that token to fetch user profile details and either create or authenticate the user in MongoDB.

After verification, I generate my own JWT/session and log the user in.
This adds strong security and removes the need for storing passwords.”

